{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.065,
   "text": "The summer I was nineteen, I ran the midnight swim at a lake camp."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.665,
   "end": 14.959,
   "text": "There was one rule. Count them going in. Count them coming out. And if the numbers don't match... don't go looking."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.759,
   "end": 20.111,
   "text": "All summer, it was easy. Twelve kids in. Twelve kids out."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.811,
   "end": 26.571,
   "text": "Then came the last night of August. No wind. The lake was flat and black, like glass."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.271,
   "end": 30.108,
   "text": "Twelve went in. I counted twice."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 31.008,
   "end": 35.744,
   "text": "When I blew the whistle, they waded back up the beach, laughing and shivering."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.144,
   "end": 38.189,
   "text": "Thirteen."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 39.789,
   "end": 45.784,
   "text": "I counted again. Thirteen dripping kids in towels... and every one of them was smiling at me."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 46.584,
   "end": 52.643,
   "text": "So I did what the rule said. I didn't look closer. I walked them to the cabins and locked the door."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 53.343,
   "end": 58.207,
   "text": "All night, I heard small wet footsteps, walking circles around the cabin."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 60.407,
   "end": 64.46,
   "text": "In the morning, I told the director we had an extra camper."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.06,
   "end": 68.943,
   "text": "She looked at her clipboard. Then at me. Very slowly."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.243,
   "end": 73.763,
   "text": "Honey... we've only had eleven campers all summer."
  }
 ],
